    "budget": "TPEx four-candidate transfer costs 12.053s, plus index 0.308s, leaving 2.639s of the shared 15s before CPU parsing/verification, raw hashing and host contention. TWSE metadata is 3.533s plus index. Per-step CPU and network were not recorded on the host; these are explicit lower-bound model costs, not invented hosted timings.",
    "controller_interval": "The 60s interval is a sleep after a tick, not a per-source guarantee. A missing/failed/ineligible continuation falls back to the 600s finished-source cadence and least-attempted rotation. The quoted 12-18 minute gaps are consistent with that fallback plus tick/host delays. In candidate source a successful, eligible persisted continuation should already request 1s sleeps; the provided receipts do NOT contain fetch-state flags, controller result/error timestamps or loop invocations, so which hosted gate failed cannot be established from them alone.",
    "controller_change": "Explicit newest-session continuations outrank ordinary due sources. Reuse the already validated terminal readback with this tick's admitted adapter bindings instead of fetching another readback and registry after persistence. Failed/degraded/unoffered sources retain existing fail-closed cadence gates.",
    "index_policy": "Index is freshly read every pull (including cache hits), at 504KB/0.308s modelled remote cost. It is already size-bounded at 8MiB and is not the dominant read; no TTL that could hide a new run was introduced.",
    "hosted_gap_followup": "Authorized hosted verifier must correlate source receipts with controller tick results and fetch_state.collector_outcome.observed for the exact deployed identity. This author has no VM/SSH/deployment authority and makes no claim of having proved the historical gap cause."
